text:
Beloved, the breeze says

your pure white garment...

My eyes will not see you;

my heart awaits you!


The wind has brought me

your name in the morning;

the echo of your steps

the mountain repeats...

my eyes will not see you;

my heart awaits you!


In the shadowy towers

the bells are ringing...

My eyes will not see you;

my heart awaits you!


The blows of the hammer

tell of the black box;

and the place of the grave,

the blows of the hoe...

My eyes will not see you;

my heart awaits you!
